Shim + Fasta fail-fast patch for Rowan (frozen Spec/Shim.lean: NOT applied).   git apply Testing/notes/audit_medium_patches/shim_fasta_failfast.patch
Base: festive-fermi 5845b97. Touches Spec/Fasta.lean + Proofs/Fasta.lean (mirror), Spec/Shim.lean + Main.lean (mirror), Spec/FROZEN.sha256 (new Shim checksum).
Independent of Fastq/Sam: applies before or after Testing/notes/shim_speed.patch (both orders checked with `git apply --check`).
Changes (audit findings 6, 10, 11, 14; details in Testing/notes/AUDIT_MEDIUM_FIXES.md):
- readFasta: name = header up to the first space or tab; throw on an empty name, on a letter outside A C G T N, on sequence before the first '>'.
- sidecar: first line "#index<TAB>size<TAB>FNV-1a64(index)"; readChromosomeList path index throws if it does not match or a line is malformed (toNat?, no toNat!).
- Shim: MIN/MAX_FRAGMENT parsed with toNat? and thrown on; SAM written to OUT.part and renamed at the end.
Checked with this patch applied: CI_check.sh passes (FUZZ=1: no violations); SAM byte-identical to the unpatched binary on the fuzz set (600 records)
and on the first 20k NovaSeq pairs (40000 records; sidecar regenerated in the new format). Old sidecars are rejected: re-run `build`.

